47
00:04:58.096 --> 00:05:02.778
<v Maya>And when human evaluators later read those letters, it resulted in systemic discrimination.</v>

48
00:05:03.199 --> 00:05:05.660
<v Daniel>OK, so the AI wrote it, but a human read it.</v>

49
00:05:05.740 --> 00:05:06.240
<v Maya>Precisely.</v>

50
00:05:06.740 --> 00:05:18.864
<v Daniel>And what this new PNAS paper adds to the literature is, well, the final iteration of that loop. The machine is no longer just writing the document for a human to read. The machine is sitting on both sides of the desk.</v>

51
00:05:19.224 --> 00:05:19.445
<v Maya>Wow.</v>

52
00:05:20.545 --> 00:05:31.931
<v Daniel>So let's look at the data on what the AI actually wrote, because I dug into those numbers and they are just wild. Remember, they stripped all explicit gender markers out of these 35,000 CVs. No pronouns, no names.</v>

